The random-forest and logistic-regression separation scores of a dimensionality-reduction evaluation accept text labels again. With scikit-learn 1.9 a random forest with `class_weight="balanced"` fails on text labels ("The classes, [...], are not in class_weight"), so every evaluation that asked for `separation_rf_balanced_accuracy` on such labels failed. Labels are now encoded as integers before the cross-validation; the scores do not change.
